#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Qiskit to implement ideas from the single-systems lesson."
msgstr "Menggunakan Qiskit untuk mengimplementasikan ide-ide dari pelajaran sistem tunggal."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation"
msgstr "Implementasi Qiskit"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll take a look at some Qiskit implementations of the concepts introduced in this lesson.\n"
"If you wish to run these implementations yourself, which is strongly encouraged, consult the [Install Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) page in the\n"
"[IBM Quantum Documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com) for details on how to set up Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bagian ini, kita akan melihat beberapa implementasi Qiskit dari konsep-konsep yang diperkenalkan dalam pelajaran ini.\n"
"Jika kamu ingin menjalankan implementasi ini sendiri, yang sangat disarankan, lihat halaman [Install Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) di\n"
"[IBM Quantum Documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com) untuk detail cara menyiapkan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It should be understood that Qiskit is under continual development, and is principally focused on maximizing the performance of the quantum computers it is used to operate, which themselves continue to evolve.\n"
"As a result, Qiskit is subject to changes that may occasionally lead to code deprecation.\n"
"With this in mind, we'll always execute the following commands prior to presenting examples of Qiskit code in this course, so that it is clear which version of Qiskit has been used.\n"
"Starting with Qiskit v1.0, this is a simple way to see what version of Qiskit is currently installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu dipahami bahwa Qiskit terus dikembangkan, dan terutama berfokus pada memaksimalkan kinerja komputer kuantum yang dioperasikannya, yang juga terus berkembang.\n"
"Akibatnya, Qiskit dapat mengalami perubahan yang sesekali mengakibatkan deprecation kode.\n"
"Dengan mempertimbangkan hal ini, kita selalu akan menjalankan perintah berikut sebelum menyajikan contoh kode Qiskit dalam kursus ini, sehingga jelas versi Qiskit mana yang digunakan.\n"
"Mulai dari Qiskit v1.0, ini adalah cara sederhana untuk melihat versi Qiskit yang saat ini terinstal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you are running this in a cloud-based Python environment, you might need to install some of the following packages:\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu menjalankan ini di lingkungan Python berbasis cloud, kamu mungkin perlu menginstal beberapa paket berikut:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vectors and matrices in Python {#vectors-and-matrices-in-python}"
msgstr "Vektor dan matriks di Python {#vectors-and-matrices-in-python}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit uses the Python programming language, so before discussing Qiskit specifically, it may be helpful to very briefly discuss matrix and vector computations in Python.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit menggunakan bahasa pemrograman Python, jadi sebelum membahas Qiskit secara khusus, mungkin berguna untuk membahas secara singkat komputasi matriks dan vektor di Python.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Python, matrix and vector computations can be performed using the `array` class from the `NumPy` library, which provides functionality for many numerical and scientific computations.\n"
"The following code loads this library, defines two column vectors, `ket0` and `ket1`, corresponding to the qubit state vectors $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$, and then prints their average.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di Python, komputasi matriks dan vektor bisa dilakukan menggunakan kelas `array` dari pustaka `NumPy`, yang menyediakan fungsionalitas untuk banyak komputasi numerik dan ilmiah.\n"
"Kode berikut memuat pustaka ini, mendefinisikan dua vektor kolom, `ket0` dan `ket1`, yang sesuai dengan vektor keadaan qubit $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 1\\rangle$, lalu mencetak rata-ratanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also use `array` to create matrices that can represent operations.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga bisa menggunakan `array` untuk membuat matriks yang bisa merepresentasikan operasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that all code appearing within a given lesson in this course is expected to be run sequentially.\n"
"Therefore, we don't need to import `NumPy` again here, because it has already been imported.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu dicatat bahwa semua kode yang muncul dalam pelajaran tertentu dalam kursus ini diharapkan dijalankan secara berurutan.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, kita tidak perlu mengimpor `NumPy` lagi di sini, karena sudah diimpor sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrix multiplication, including matrix-vector multiplication as a special case, can be performed using the `@` operator.\n"
msgstr "Perkalian matriks, termasuk perkalian matriks-vektor sebagai kasus khusus, bisa dilakukan menggunakan operator `@`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This output formatting leaves something to be desired, visually speaking.\n"
"One solution, for situations that demand something prettier, is to use the`array_to_latex` function in Qiskit, from the `qiskit.visualization` module.\n"
"Note that, in the code that follows, we're using Python's generic `display` function (especially in notebooks), because it can render objects using richer representations, whereas `print()` simply uses the object's string representation. This is similar to how `NumPy` arrays provide their own specialized formatting while Python lists use the default list representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Format output ini masih kurang ideal, secara visual.\n"
"Salah satu solusi, untuk situasi yang membutuhkan tampilan yang lebih indah, adalah menggunakan fungsi `array_to_latex` di Qiskit, dari modul `qiskit.visualization`.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa, dalam kode berikut, kita menggunakan fungsi generik `display` dari Python (terutama di notebook), karena fungsi ini bisa merender objek menggunakan representasi yang lebih kaya, sedangkan `print()` hanya menggunakan representasi string dari objek tersebut. Ini mirip dengan bagaimana array `NumPy` menyediakan formatting khususnya sendiri sedangkan list Python menggunakan representasi list default.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1  \\\\\n"
" 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1  \\\\\n"
" 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & \\frac{3}{4}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & \\frac{3}{4}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "States, measurements, and operations {#states-measurements-and-operations}"
msgstr "Keadaan, pengukuran, dan operasi {#states-measurements-and-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit includes several classes that allow for states, measurements, and operations to be created and manipulated — so there is no need to program everything required to simulate quantum states, measurements, and operations in Python.\n"
"Some examples to help you to get started are included below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit menyertakan beberapa kelas yang memungkinkan keadaan, pengukuran, dan operasi dibuat dan dimanipulasi — sehingga tidak perlu memprogram semua yang diperlukan untuk mensimulasikan keadaan kuantum, pengukuran, dan operasi di Python.\n"
"Beberapa contoh untuk membantu kamu memulai disertakan di bawah ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define and display state vectors {#define-and-display-state-vectors}"
msgstr "Mendefinisikan dan menampilkan vektor keadaan {#define-and-display-state-vectors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The`Statevector` class in Qiskit provides functionality for defining and manipulating quantum state vectors.\n"
"In the code that follows, the `Statevector` class is imported and a few vectors are defined.\n"
"(We're also importing the `sqrt` function from the `NumPy` library to compute a square root.\n"
"This function could, alternatively, be called as `np.sqrt` provided that `NumPy` has already been imported, as it has above; this is merely a different way to import and use this specific function alone.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `Statevector` di Qiskit menyediakan fungsionalitas untuk mendefinisikan dan memanipulasi vektor keadaan kuantum.\n"
"Dalam kode berikut, kelas `Statevector` diimpor dan beberapa vektor didefinisikan.\n"
"(Kita juga mengimpor fungsi `sqrt` dari pustaka `NumPy` untuk menghitung akar kuadrat.\n"
"Fungsi ini, sebagai alternatif, bisa dipanggil sebagai `np.sqrt` asalkan `NumPy` sudah diimpor, seperti yang telah dilakukan di atas; ini hanyalah cara berbeda untuk mengimpor dan menggunakan fungsi spesifik ini saja.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Statevector` class includes a `draw` method for displaying state vectors in a variety of ways, including\n"
"`text` for plain text, `latex` for rendered LaTeX, and `latex_source` for LaTeX code, which can be handy for cutting and pasting into documents.\n"
"(Use `print` rather than `display` to show LaTeX code for best results.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `Statevector` menyertakan metode `draw` untuk menampilkan vektor keadaan dengan berbagai cara, termasuk\n"
"`text` untuk teks biasa, `latex` untuk LaTeX yang dirender, dan `latex_source` untuk kode LaTeX, yang berguna untuk disalin dan ditempel ke dokumen.\n"
"(Gunakan `print` daripada `display` untuk menampilkan kode LaTeX dengan hasil terbaik.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |0\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Statevector` class also includes the `is_valid` method, which checks to see if a given vector is a valid quantum state vector (in other words, that it has Euclidean norm equal to 1):\n"
msgstr "Kelas `Statevector` juga menyertakan metode `is_valid`, yang memeriksa apakah vektor yang diberikan adalah vektor keadaan kuantum yang valid (dengan kata lain, bahwa ia memiliki norma Euclidean sama dengan 1):\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulating measurements using `Statevector` {#simulating-measurements-using-statevector}"
msgstr "Mensimulasikan pengukuran menggunakan `Statevector` {#simulating-measurements-using-statevector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we will see one way that measurements of quantum states can be simulated in Qiskit, using the `measure` method from the `Statevector` class.\n"
"Let's use the same qubit state vector `v` defined previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya kita akan melihat salah satu cara pengukuran keadaan kuantum bisa disimulasikan di Qiskit, menggunakan metode `measure` dari kelas `Statevector`.\n"
"Mari kita gunakan vektor keadaan qubit `v` yang sama yang didefinisikan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2 i}{3}) |0\\rangle- \\frac{2}{3} |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2 i}{3}) |0\\rangle- \\frac{2}{3} |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Running the `measure` method simulates a standard basis measurement.\n"
"It returns the outcome of that measurement, plus the new quantum state vector of the system after the measurement.\n"
"(Here we're using Python's `print` function with an `f` prefix for formatted printing with embedded expressions.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Menjalankan metode `measure` mensimulasikan pengukuran basis standar.\n"
"Ini mengembalikan hasil pengukuran tersebut, ditambah vektor keadaan kuantum baru dari sistem setelah pengukuran.\n"
"(Di sini kita menggunakan fungsi `print` Python dengan awalan `f` untuk pencetakan terformat dengan ekspresi yang disematkan.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$- |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$- |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Measurement outcomes are probabilistic, so this method can return different results when run multiple times.\n"
"For the particular example of the vector `v` defined above, the `measure` method defines the quantum state vector after the measurement takes place to be\n"
msgstr ""
"Hasil pengukuran bersifat probabilistik, sehingga metode ini bisa mengembalikan hasil yang berbeda saat dijalankan beberapa kali.\n"
"Untuk contoh khusus vektor `v` yang didefinisikan di atas, metode `measure` mendefinisikan vektor keadaan kuantum setelah pengukuran menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{1 + 2i}{\\sqrt{5}}\\biggr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{1 + 2i}{\\sqrt{5}}\\biggr) \\vert 0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(rather than $\\vert 0\\rangle$) or\n"
msgstr "(bukan $\\vert 0\\rangle$) atau\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"- \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"- \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(rather than $\\vert 1\\rangle$), depending on the measurement outcome.\n"
"In both cases, the alternatives to $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle$ are, in fact, equivalent to these state vectors; they are said to to *equivalent up to a global phase* because one is equal to the other multiplied by a complex number on the unit circle.\n"
"This issue is discussed in greater detail in the [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) lesson, and can safely be ignored for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"(bukan $\\vert 1\\rangle$), tergantung pada hasil pengukuran.\n"
"Dalam kedua kasus, alternatif dari $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dan $\\vert 1\\rangle$ sebenarnya setara dengan vektor keadaan tersebut; dikatakan *ekuivalen hingga fase global* karena satu sama dengan yang lain dikalikan dengan bilangan kompleks pada lingkaran satuan.\n"
"Masalah ini dibahas lebih rinci dalam pelajaran [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction), dan untuk saat ini bisa diabaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Statevector` will throw an error if the `measure` method is applied to an invalid quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr "`Statevector` akan menghasilkan error jika metode `measure` diterapkan pada vektor keadaan kuantum yang tidak valid.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Statevector` also comes with a `sample_counts` method that allows for the simulation of any number of measurements on the system, each time starting with a fresh copy of the state. For example, the following code shows the outcome of measuring the vector `v` $1000$ times, which (with high probability) results in the outcome $0$ approximately $5$ out of every $9$ times (or about $556$ of the $1000$ trials) and the outcome $1$ approximately $4$ out of every $9$ times (or about $444$ out of the $1000$ trials).\n"
"The code that follows also demonstrates the `plot_histogram` function from the `qiskit.visualization` module for visualizing the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Statevector` juga dilengkapi metode `sample_counts` yang memungkinkan simulasi sejumlah pengukuran pada sistem, setiap kali dimulai dengan salinan baru dari keadaan. Misalnya, kode berikut menunjukkan hasil pengukuran vektor `v` sebanyak $1000$ kali, yang (dengan probabilitas tinggi) menghasilkan hasil $0$ kira-kira $5$ dari setiap $9$ kali (atau sekitar $556$ dari $1000$ percobaan) dan hasil $1$ kira-kira $4$ dari setiap $9$ kali (atau sekitar $444$ dari $1000$ percobaan).\n"
"Kode berikut juga mendemonstrasikan fungsi `plot_histogram` dari modul `qiskit.visualization` untuk memvisualisasikan hasilnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/fde6ccf9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/fde6ccf9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Running this code on your own multiple times, with different numbers of samples in place of $1000$, may be helpful for developing some intuition for how the number of trials influences the number of times each outcome appears.\n"
"With more and more samples, the fraction of samples for each possibility is likely to get closer and closer to the corresponding probability.\n"
"This phenomenon, more generally speaking, is known as the *law of large numbers* in probability theory.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menjalankan kode ini sendiri beberapa kali, dengan jumlah sampel yang berbeda sebagai pengganti $1000$, mungkin berguna untuk mengembangkan intuisi tentang bagaimana jumlah percobaan mempengaruhi berapa kali setiap hasil muncul.\n"
"Dengan semakin banyak sampel, fraksi sampel untuk setiap kemungkinan cenderung semakin mendekati probabilitas yang bersesuaian.\n"
"Fenomena ini, secara lebih umum, dikenal sebagai *hukum bilangan besar* dalam teori probabilitas.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perform operations with `Operator` and `Statevector` {#perform-operations-with-operator-and-statevector}"
msgstr "Melakukan operasi dengan `Operator` dan `Statevector` {#perform-operations-with-operator-and-statevector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary operations can be defined in Qiskit using the `Operator` class, as in the example that follows.\n"
"This class includes a `draw` method with similar arguments to `Statevector`.\n"
"Note that the `latex` option produces results equivalent to `array_to_latex`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi uniter bisa didefinisikan di Qiskit menggunakan kelas `Operator`, seperti dalam contoh berikut.\n"
"Kelas ini menyertakan metode `draw` dengan argumen serupa dengan `Statevector`.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa opsi `latex` menghasilkan hasil yang setara dengan `array_to_latex`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can apply a unitary operation to a state vector using the `evolve` method.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa menerapkan operasi uniter pada vektor keadaan menggunakan metode `evolve`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$(0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i) |0\\rangle+(-0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i) |1\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$(0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i) |0\\rangle+(-0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i) |1\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A preview of quantum circuits {#a-preview-of-quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Pratinjau sirkuit kuantum {#a-preview-of-quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits won't be formally introduced until the [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) lesson, which is the third lesson in this course, but we can nevertheless experiment with composing qubit unitary operations using the`QuantumCircuit` class in Qiskit.\n"
"In particular, we may define a quantum circuit (which, in this case, will simply be a sequence of unitary operations performed on a single qubit) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sirkuit kuantum tidak akan diperkenalkan secara formal sampai pelajaran [Quantum circuits](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction), yang merupakan pelajaran ketiga dalam kursus ini, tapi kita tetap bisa bereksperimen dengan mengomposisikan operasi uniter qubit menggunakan kelas `QuantumCircuit` di Qiskit.\n"
"Secara khusus, kita bisa mendefinisikan sirkuit kuantum (yang, dalam kasus ini, hanyalah urutan operasi uniter yang dilakukan pada satu qubit) sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/68490946-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/qiskit-implementation/extracted-outputs/68490946-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using the `draw` method from the `QuantumCircuit` class with the `mpl` renderer (short for `Matplotlib`, a Python visualization library).\n"
"This is the only renderer we'll use for quantum circuits in this course, but there are other options, including a text-based and a LaTeX-based renderer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita menggunakan metode `draw` dari kelas `QuantumCircuit` dengan renderer `mpl` (singkatan dari `Matplotlib`, pustaka visualisasi Python).\n"
"Ini adalah satu-satunya renderer yang akan kita gunakan untuk sirkuit kuantum dalam kursus ini, tapi ada opsi lain, termasuk renderer berbasis teks dan berbasis LaTeX.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operations are applied sequentially, starting on the left and ending on the right in the diagram.\n"
"A handy way to get the unitary matrix corresponding to this circuit is to use the `from_circuit` method from the `Operator` class.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi diterapkan secara berurutan, dimulai dari kiri dan berakhir di kanan dalam diagram.\n"
"Cara praktis untuk mendapatkan matriks uniter yang sesuai dengan sirkuit ini adalah menggunakan metode `from_circuit` dari kelas `Operator`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i & 0.8535533906 + 0.3535533906 i  \\\\\n"
" -0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i & 0.3535533906 + 0.1464466094 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0.1464466094 - 0.3535533906 i & 0.8535533906 + 0.3535533906 i  \\\\\n"
" -0.3535533906 + 0.8535533906 i & 0.3535533906 + 0.1464466094 i  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also initialize a starting quantum state vector and then evolve that state according to the sequence of operations described by the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kita juga bisa menginisialisasi vektor keadaan kuantum awal dan kemudian mengevolusi keadaan itu sesuai dengan urutan operasi yang dijelaskan oleh sirkuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
